  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 152 AM MDT Sun Jul 12 2026\n\nMostly dry conditions expected today and into Monday as well. A\nmonsoon push of moisture is trying to work around the center of\na high pressure area now situated to our east. Models are \nindicating a few virga showers possible across the eastern \nhighlands this afternoon. Confidence isn't strong enough to \nmention them in the forecast. Potential a few more of these \nshowers on Monday across the high country but once again low \nconfidence at this time. The bigger impacts for today and \ntomorrow are the heat. We've upgraded several heat advisories \ninto warnings now that models are consistently forecasting highs\nnear all-time records and heat risk values are showing a few \nmore 3s and 4s which point to potentially more severe impacts. \nAm concerned if high cirrus or even a few cumulus build-up could\nrestrict us from reaching these temps, but models have been \nvery consistent with the cloud cover as well. Temps are just a \ntouch cooler Monday as the center of the high moves further into\nthe northern Plains. \n\n\nAs we move into Monday night and Tuesday, we see a stronger push of \nmoisture moving into the region. Expect isolated to scattered \nshowers and thunderstorms across central Idaho. Temps are a couple \ndegrees cooler with additional cloud cover and the high moving \nfurther away. As we move into middle and late week, the main story \nwill be thunderstorm potential with the monsoon flow nearby. \nAnticipating that some heavy rain could be possible if the \nmonsoon sets squarely up on top of us. Temps continue to look warm \nthrough late week with many lower elevations seeing highs in the \nlower and mid 90s.",
